Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Fault Injection Not Working
If fault injection isn't working as expected:

# Check if virtual service is applied correctly
kubectl get virtualservice -o yaml

# Verify Istio sidecar is injected
kubectl get pods -o jsonpath='{.items[*].spec.containers[*].name}'

# Check Istio proxy configuration
kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -c istio-proxy -- pilot-agent request GET config_dump
Issue 2: Monitoring Tools Not Accessible
If monitoring dashboards are not accessible:

# Check if monitoring services are running
kubectl get pods -n istio-system | grep -E "(grafana|prometheus|jaeger|kiali)"

# Verify port forwarding
ps aux | grep "port-forward"

# Restart port forwarding if needed
pkill -f "port-forward"
kubectl -n istio-system port-forward svc/grafana 3000:3000 &
Issue 3: High Resource Usage
If the cluster becomes unresponsive:

# Check resource usage
kubectl top nodes
kubectl top pods --all-namespaces

# Scale down traffic generation
pkill -f "generate-traffic"

# Remove fault injection temporarily
kubectl delete virtualservice ratings-combined
Cleanup
Clean up the lab environment:

# Remove fault injection configurations
kubectl delete virtualservice --all
kubectl delete destinationrule --all

# Stop port forwarding
pkill -f "port-forward"

# Remove generated files
rm -f *.yaml *.sh

echo "Lab cleanup completed"
